          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            At certain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo =
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s = n
            the values
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(s)
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-functions"} L-functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            are typically of special interest, these are known as the “special values of L-functions”.
          %p
            For instance some of special values of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+zeta+function"} Riemann zeta function
            found (for the non-trivial region of non-positive integers) by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonhard+Euler"} Leonhard Euler
            in 1734 and 1749 are
          %table
            %thead
              %tr
                %th n
                %th -5
                %th -3
                %th -1
                %th 0
                %th 2
                %th 4
                %th 6
                %th 8
            %tbody
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ζ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \zeta(n)
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mfrac
                          %mn 1
                          %mn 252
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -\frac{1}{252}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
